All 33 tests pass, and only `src/dispatcher.js` and `test/dispatcher.test.js` were modified.

I extended `dispatch` with the three new options. Validation happens before the drain loop, so an invalid `maxAttempts` (not a positive integer) or `baseDelayMs` (not a non-negative integer) throws `RangeError` with the queue untouched. Each job is attempted up to `maxAttempts` times; after a failed attempt that has a successor, it awaits `sleep(baseDelayMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1))`. Every `processed`/`failed` entry now carries `attempts`, each job logs exactly once at its final outcome in the existing format, and `total` remains the job count. The injected-`sleep` tests cover retry-then-succeed, exhaustion with the last error, backoff timing `[100, 200, 400]`, the `maxAttempts: 1` no-sleep path, and pre-dequeue validation.
